            <ArticleTitle>Effects of long-term corn consumption on brain serotonin and the response to electric shock.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>692-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rats fed tryptophan-poor corn diets have reduced levels of brain serotonin and show increased responsiveness to electric shock. This diet-induced hyperalgesia can be reversed by feeding the animals diets with adequate amounts of tryptophan, or by systemic injections of the amino acid.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
